ra: solicit again before the router lifetime expires

odhcp6c only sends Router Solicitations at startup and on carrier changes.
A router that answers solicitations but never sends unsolicited RAs, like
the FM350-GL cellular modem (router lifetime 21840 s), therefore loses its
default route one router lifetime after the connect; odhcpd then advertises
router lifetime 0 on the LAN. Re-arm the RS timer at half the router
lifetime on every RA with a non-zero lifetime; routers that send periodic
RAs push it out before it fires.

--- a/src/ra.c	2022-08-01 19:27:51.000000000 +0000
+++ b/src/ra.c	2026-09-24 23:37:30.254873885 +0000
@@ -423,9 +423,17 @@
 		 * Moreover, a host SHOULD send at least one solicitation in the case
 		 * where an advertisement is received prior to having sent a solicitation.
 		 */
-		if (rs_attempt > 0 && router_valid > 0) {
-			alarm(0);
+		if (router_valid > 0) {
 			rs_attempt = 0;
+			/*
+			 * Some routers answer solicitations but never send
+			 * unsolicited RAs (e.g. the Fibocom FM350-GL cellular
+			 * modem), so the default route would expire after one
+			 * router lifetime. Solicit again at half the lifetime;
+			 * a periodic RA from a normal router re-arms the timer
+			 * first. This also stops pending RS retransmissions.
+			 */
+			alarm(router_valid / 2);
 		}
 
 		// Parse default route
